From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gles2_debayer: apply the colour steps in the right order

The preview shader does "color *= color_matrix" with the row-major matrix
uploaded untransposed, which works out to colormat * rgb, so
the matrix has to be XYZ->sRGB * D50->D65 * ForwardMatrix * WB. It was
built the other way round, WB * Forward * D50->D65 * XYZ->sRGB. With
the default calibration both orders give the identity, which hid it; with
a real DCP a white surface came out (0.70, 1.15, 0.56) instead of white,
and auto white balance then pulled the whole preview orange.

---
--- a/src/gles2_debayer.c	2026-10-08 23:06:03.312934600 +0400
+++ b/src/gles2_debayer.c	2026-10-08 23:06:03.359331720 +0400
@@ -177,9 +177,14 @@
                 float colormat[9];
                 float xyz[9];
                 float xyzd65[9];
-                multiply_matrices(wb, self->forward_matrix, xyz);
-                multiply_matrices(xyz, XYZD50_to_D65, xyzd65);
-                multiply_matrices(xyzd65, XYZD65_to_sRGB, colormat);
+                /*
+                 * The shader computes colormat * rgb, so the steps apply
+                 * right to left: white balance, then the forward matrix
+                 * (camera to XYZ D50), then D50 to D65, then XYZ to sRGB.
+                 */
+                multiply_matrices(self->forward_matrix, wb, xyz);
+                multiply_matrices(XYZD50_to_D65, xyz, xyzd65);
+                multiply_matrices(XYZD65_to_sRGB, xyzd65, colormat);
                 glUniformMatrix3fv(
                         self->uniform_color_matrix, 1, GL_FALSE, colormat);
         } else if (self->shader == SHADER_YUV) {
